    "6": {
      "said": "Generous drivable par 4, plays about 230; elsewhere it'd be a par 3. I go for it with hybrid and make a lot of birdies. Bunkers along the right side, but short-right off the tee is totally fine and gives a really wide green to hit into: 170-210 off the tee on the right, even 10 yds right of the fairway, is fine. Short is fine off the tee. Left/long-left is dead (trees). Left around the green is not a great place. Beyond the green is dead once you're hitting your approach (green runs away). Off the tee you really want to be short: short-left, short-right.",
      "notes": [
        "Drivable. Going for it with hybrid has made a lot of birdies.",
